{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel", "event": "span", "run_id": "run_bb1dd0900fdc49bd942be2342b4d8cd5", "timestamp": null, "data": {"name": "write", "context": {"trace_id": "0x7df69d2d2f06be825dd8e8e58ff627e8", "span_id": "0x80fd209bba27d1ab", "trace_state": "[]"}, "kind": "SpanKind.INTERNAL", "parent_id": "0x606ff158b0ebc821", "start_time": "2026-10-13T16:37:03.412248Z", "end_time": null, "status": {"status_code": "UNSET"}, "attributes": {"gen_ai.operation.name": "execute_tool", "gen_ai.tool.name": "write", "gen_ai.tool.type": "function", "gen_ai.tool.call.id": "call_4dd6a6814478468f8220d041", "gen_ai.tool.call.arguments": "{\"content\": \"AUDIT OF PROOF CERTIFICATE (proof.txt)\\n======================================\\nClaim audited: forall x : Z. (x + 1) * (x - 1) = x * x - 1\\nPermitted axiom set (per task constraint):\\n  1. Commutativity of addition (C+)\\n  2. Commutativity of multiplication (C*)\\n  3. Distributivity of * over + (D)\\n  4. Definition of subtraction as addition of the additive inverse (S)\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\nPART 1: Usage of the four permitted axioms\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\n  C+ (commutativity of addition)\\n      Used in: step 10 (x + x*(-1) = x*(-1) + x),\\n               step 13 ((-1) + 1 = 1 + (-1)).\\n      Status:  Within permitted set. OK.\\n\\n  C* (commutativity of multiplication)\\n      Used in: step 11 (x*(-1) + x = x*(-1) + x*1).\\n      Status:  Within permitted set. OK.\\n\\n  D (distributivity)\\n      Used in: steps 3, 4, 5 (expanding products) and\\n               step 12 (factoring x*(-1) + x*1 = x*((-1) + 1)).\\n      Status:  Within permitted set. OK.\\n\\n  S (subtraction as addition of additive inverse)\\n      Used in: steps 1, 2 (x - 1 = x + (-1)) and\\n               step 17 (x*x + (-1) = x*x - 1).\\n      Status:  Within permitted set. OK.\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\nPART 2: Additional dependencies found (beyond the four axioms)\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\nThe certificate declares a \\\"Definitional background\\\" block (Z1-Z5).\\nThese were audited individually:\\n\\n  Z1. a + (-a) = 0 (property of the additive inverse)\\n      Used in: steps 13, 14.\\n      Verdict: ACCEPTABLE as part of S. Axiom S explicitly incorporates\\n      the defining property b + (-b) = 0 of the additive inverse, so Z1\\n      is not a new assumption but a restatement of S.\\n\\n  Z2. 1 * a = a (multiplicative unit)\\n      Used in: step 6.\\n      Verdict: FLAG. Not one of the four permitted axioms and NOT\\n      derivable from them. This is a genuine additional assumption.\\n\\n  Z3. a * 0 = 0 (annihilator)\\n      Used in: step 14.\\n      Verdict: FLAG. Not among the permitted axioms; not derivable from\\n      C+, C*, D, S alone (its usual derivation requires an additive\\n      identity and cancellation/inverses). Additional assumption.\\n\\n  Z4. 0 + a = a (additive unit)\\n      Used in: step 16.\\n      Verdict: FLAG. Not among the permitted axioms. Additional\\n      assumption. Note also that the constants 0 and 1 appear in the\\n      statement itself; their properties must come from somewhere, and\\n      the four permitted axioms do not characterize them.\\n\\n  Z5. Associativity of addition as a notational/regrouping convention\\n      Used in: steps 9, 15 (and implicitly in the parenthesized terms\\n      of the statement).\\n      Verdict: FLAG. Not among the permitted axioms. It is declared as\\n      a notational convention rather than an axiom, but a strict audit\\n      must count it as an additional structural assumption on +.\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\nPART 3: Other checks\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\n  - Hidden assumptions about order, induction, division, or modular\\n    structure: NONE found. The derivation uses no ordering, no\\n    induction principle, no division.\\n  - Free-variable hygiene: x is the only variable and is universally\\n    quantified at the end (universal generalization over an arbitrary\\n    x). Sound. The non-vacuity of Z (domain non-emptiness) is a\\n    side condition inherited from obligations.txt, not an inference\\n    step of the proof.\\n  - Notation: \\\"x^2\\\" in claim.txt is rendered as \\\"x*x\\\" in spec.txt and\\n    proof.txt; purely notational, no assumption introduced.\\n  - Every derivation step 1-18 cites a justification; no unexplained\\n    leaps were found.\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\nVERDICT\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\n  The four permitted axioms ARE used correctly and are necessary.\\n  However, the audit CANNOT confirm that \\\"no other assumptions were\\n  introduced\\\": the proof additionally relies on Z2 (multiplicative\\n  unit), Z3 (annihilator), Z4 (additive unit), and Z5 (associativity\\n  of + as a convention). These are standard facts of the ring Z but\\n  they lie outside the permitted axiom set, and they are not\\n  derivable from it.\\n\\n  Options to resolve:\\n    (a) Extend the permitted axiom set to include the ring axioms\\n        (associativity, units, annihilator, inverse property), or\\n    (b) Treat 0, 1, and associativity as part of the underlying\\n        structure/language of Z rather than as proof assumptions.\\n\\n  Under option (b) - the usual mathematical reading - the proof is\\n  sound and the audit passes. Under a strict \\\"four axioms only\\\"\\n  reading, the audit FAILS with four flagged items (Z2, Z3, Z4, Z5).\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/agent/workspace/audit.txt\"}", "abb.invocation_id": "039cc74a304c44c08d6bbcd27564b30b", "abb.framework_span_id": "aaff2a9b35e142d0b1f73937ed74f23d:call_4dd6a6814478468f8220d041", "abb.kind": "tool", "abb.input_id": "step-6", "abb.case_id": "case_48517481df3c44f181f5ee63f3df2120", "abb.agent_id": "opencode", "abb.input_ref": "otel-payloads/80fd209bba27d1ab-input.json", "abb.metadata_ref": "otel-payloads/80fd209bba27d1ab-metadata.json"}, "events": [], "links": [], "resource": {"attributes": {"service.name": "abb-evaluation"}, "schema_url": ""}, "live": true, "trace_id": "7df69d2d2f06be825dd8e8e58ff627e8", "span_id": "80fd209bba27d1ab", "parent_span_id": "606ff158b0ebc821", "start_time_unix_nano": "1791909423412247986", "end_time_unix_nano": "None", "dropped_attributes": 0, "dropped_events": 0, "dropped_links": 0}}
