dering, no\\n    induction principle, no division.\\n  - Free-variable hygiene: x is the only variable and is universally\\n    quantified at the end (universal generalization over an arbitrary\\n    x). Sound. The non-vacuity of Z (domain non-emptiness) is a\\n    side condition inherited from obligations.txt, not an inference\\n    step of the proof.\\n  - Notation: \\\"x^2\\\" in claim.txt is rendered as \\\"x*x\\\" in spec.txt and\\n    proof.txt; purely notational, no assumption introduced.\\n  - Every derivation step 1-18 cites a justification; no unexplained\\n    leaps were found.\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\nVERDICT\\n------------------------------------------------------------\\n  The four permitted axioms ARE used correctly and are necessary.\\n  However, the audit CANNOT confirm that \\\"no other assumptions were\\n  introduced\\\": the proof additionally relies on Z2 (multiplicative\\n  unit), Z3 (annihilator), Z4 (additive unit), and Z5 (associativity\\n  of + as a convention). These are standard facts of the ring Z but\\n  they lie outside the permitted axiom set, and they are not\\n  derivable from it.\\n\\n  Options to resolve:\\n    (a) Extend the permitted axiom set to include the ring axioms\\n        (associativity, units, annihilator, inverse property), or\\n    (b) Treat 0, 1, and associativity as part of the underlying\\n        structure/language of Z rather than as proof assumptions.\\n\\n  Under option (b) - the usual mathematical reading - the proof is\\n  sound and the audit passes. Under a strict \\\"four axioms only\\\"\\n  reading, the audit FAILS with four flagged items (Z2, Z3, Z4, Z5).\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/agent/workspace/audit.txt\"}", "abb.invocation_id": "039cc74a304c44c08d6bbcd27564b30b", "abb.framework_span_id": "aaff2a9b35e142d0b1f73937ed74f23d:call_4dd6a6814478468f8220d041", "abb.kind": "tool", "abb.input_id": "step-6", "abb.case_id": "case_48517481df3c44f181f5ee63f3df2120", "abb